  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Finely shred the cabbage. Peel the carrot, then shred using a julienne peeler or coarsely grate with a box grater. Halve the cucumber lengthwise, scrape out the seeds using a teaspoon (see Make it faster), then thinly slice on an angle. Finely chop the mint leaves, discarding the stems. Crush or finely chop 1 small garlic clove.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156630/photos/large/prep_ingredients-24579747fbc1c0cdd06e2c1f1367cdac.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast pepitas: Put the pepitas in a cold medium frypan over medium heat. Toast, tossing, for 3-4 mins until evenly golden. Remove from the pan and cool slightly.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156631/photos/large/toast_pepitas-48d4237770308ccfb7b81aa73e405237.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm patties: Heat 1 tbs olive oil in the same pan over medium-high heat. Cook the wholegrain patties for 3 mins each side or until golden and warmed through. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156632/photos/large/pan_fry_patties-ca3ffdcd4725f727c9e1f2ac02ec6ff6.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make salad: Meanwhile, combine 1 tbs olive oil, 1 tbs white wine vinegar, 1 tsp dijon mustard and 1 tsp honey in a large bowl. Season with salt and pepper and whisk to combine. Add the cabbage, carrot, cucumber, pepitas and half the mint to the bowl and toss well to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156633/photos/large/make_salad-e3b215954562b04fd7c01afa6fdf5b66.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Combine the yoghurt, garlic and remaining mint in a bowl and season with salt and pepper. Divide the patties among plates, top with the mint yoghurt, serve with the salad and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156634/photos/large/serve_up-ca6297556730abad95b9dc4b48749883.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it faster: We've suggested removing the seeds, as they can make the salad a bit watery. It doesn't take long to scrape them out, but if you want to cut down on a bit of prep time, leave them in.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/156635/photos/large/make_it_faster-0503ccdc3025f1e00db8e007a1cc8f00.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
